    nemotron cuda: shared windows of several sequences run the latent shared expert on the side stream again
    
    A shared window is one forward over its streams' rows: every MoE layer reads the engine's shared scratch, the cached
    plan for the window's total rows and one fork and join, as a lone window and the MTP head's batched levels already do.
    Only two ranks keep the shared expert on the main stream. tf-cuda-test shared-fork adds shared windows of 2, 4 and 8
    streams at their narrowest and widest, with the shared rows poisoned and the side stream held back.

